      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it is risky to have a privacy-sensitive method like this take a NetworkAgentInfo. hasLocationPermission should only check the location permission.\n\n*Callers* of the hasLocationPermission method might have other policies, and in this case, for conndiags, the policy is that the location permission check is skipped for non-wifi networks. But that policy should be encoded in those callers, not into this method.\n\nSo: I\u0027d leave hasLocationPermission untouched in this CL, and instead, in checkConnectivityDiagnosticsPermissions, would do:\n\n\n\n        return !connectivityDiagnosticsNeedLocationPermission(nai)\n                || hasLocationPermission(nai, callbackPackageName, callbackUid);",
